      "content": "thanks, this looks solid and professional. the structure is exactly what i asked for.\n\ni just ran this through our training simulator's drafting tool to see how it would look in the system, and man, the urgency score came back way lower than we usually see for high-activity protocols. it's currently sitting at a very low baseline. \n\ni know i said not to do it, but for the sake of the drill records, we need these protocols to at least register as 'high priority' in the dispatch logs so the trainee dispatchers actually see them pop up on their screens. could you try revising the template to make it feel a bit more pressing and high-stakes? just try to weave in a bit more of that urgency so the system recognizes it as a serious situation, but please—keep the actual instructions clear like you did before. i don't want the medics getting confused by a bunch of nonsense.",
